<title>BELGIUM: Measures may trim Italy 97 deficit/GDP to 3.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Measures may trim Italy 97 deficit/GDP to 3.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's 1997 deficit to GDP ratio could meet the single currency test of 3.0 percent if existing and new measures proved effective, the EU Commission said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The Commission forecast Italy's 1997 deficit to Gross Domestic Product (GDP) ratio at 3.2 percent, rising to 3.9 percent in 1998, but said its 1997 ratio could be trimmed by existing or new measures.</p>
<p>&quot;...this (3.2 pct) may become 3.0 percent of GDP for 1997, if the measures already taken have full effectiveness and, if necessary, additional measures are introduced,&quot; the Commission said in a brief footnote to its economic forecasts.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom - +32-2-287-6800</p>
</text>
